    "sentence_translations": [
      "(11) What Shall I Do?",
      "",
      "Old Guan disappeared. Little Dong was going to cry.",
      "",
      "Little Dong asked Dad, “Old Guan disappeared! What shall I do?”",
      "",
      "Dad said, “How could she have disappeared? What about her family?”",
      "",
      "“She is alone. She doesn’t have any family. She is very kind. She is really cool.",
      "She often talks to me, but she has disappeared …” Little Dong cried.",
      "",
      "“Don’t cry, don’t cry. Does she have a cell phone?” Dad said.",
      "",
      "“No. Her … her phone number is 0317652.",
      "She’s in Beijing. She isn’t answering my calls. It’s been five days. She … dis … disappeared,” Little Dong said.",
      "",
      "“Beijing? Calling? How did you meet?” Dad asked.",
      "",
      "“You and Mom are too busy. You are hardly at home. I am often alone.",
      "I don’t want to be alone. I want to talk. One day, I called the wrong number.",
      "I got to know Old Guan. She was able to talk with me. But now, where has she gone? She has disappeared. What shall I do?”"
    ]
  }
